{"doc_urls":["chapters/1/basics.html#basics","chapters/1/basics.html#entities","chapters/1/basics.html#components","chapters/1/basics.html#systems"],"index":{"documentStore":{"docInfo":{"0":{"body":30,"breadcrumbs":4,"title":1},"1":{"body":27,"breadcrumbs":4,"title":1},"2":{"body":43,"breadcrumbs":4,"title":1},"3":{"body":34,"breadcrumbs":4,"title":1}},"docs":{"0":{"body":"SettleTown uses Bevy , an open-source game engine. Bevy utilizes a model called ECS , which stands for Entity Component System . It is a development paradigm often associated with game development. It has a number of basic concepts associated with it, but the three main concepts are described in the title:","breadcrumbs":"Chapter 1: Basics » Basics","id":"0","title":"Basics"},"1":{"body":"Entities are data structures that store zero or more Components . They are general-purpose game-world objects. They must have a unique id, but other than that, they can be effectively empty structs. For example, a PlayerCharacter entity may exist, representing the player character for the game. struct PlayerCharacter(u64);","breadcrumbs":"Chapter 1: Basics » Entities","id":"1","title":"Entities"},"2":{"body":"Components are basic Rust structs (typically, they can also be enums or zero-sized types) that implement the Component trait. They are data structures used to store data for an Entity . In abstract terms, they are definitions that an entity contains a particular aspect. For example, the PlayerCharacter entity, from above may have a Position component, allowing it to exist somewhere in the world space. #[derive(Component)]\nstruct WorldPosition { x: f32, y: f32,\n}","breadcrumbs":"Chapter 1: Basics » Components","id":"2","title":"Components"},"3":{"body":"A System is an operation that acts on all entities having a given component. For example, with the above PlayerCharacter and WorldPosition structs, a Movement system may exist that queries the entities with a particular position and updates that position. fn update_position_system(mut query: Query<&mut WorldPosition>) { for position in &query { position.x = position.x + 1; position.y = position.y + 1; }\n}","breadcrumbs":"Chapter 1: Basics » Systems","id":"3","title":"Systems"}},"length":4,"save":true},"fields":["title","body","breadcrumbs"],"index":{"body":{"root":{"1":{"df":1,"docs":{"3":{"tf":1.4142135623730951}}},"a":{"b":{"df":0,"docs":{},"o":{"df":0,"docs":{},"v":{"df":2,"docs":{"2":{"tf":1.0},"3":{"tf":1.0}}}},"s":{"df":0,"docs":{},"t":{"df":0,"docs":{},"r":{"a":{"c":{"df":0,"docs":{},"t":{"df":1,"docs":{"2":{"tf":1.0}}}},"df":0,"docs":{}},"df":0,"docs":{}}}}},"c":{"df":0,"docs":{},"t":{"df":1,"docs":{"3":{"tf":1.0}}}},"df":0,"docs":{},"l":{"df":0,"docs":{},"l":{"df":0,"docs":{},"o":{"df":0,"docs":{},"w":{"df":1,"docs":{"2":{"tf":1.0}}}}}},"s":{"df":0,"docs":{},"p":{"df":0,"docs":{},"e":{"c":{"df":0,"docs":{},"t":{"df":1,"docs":{"2":{"tf":1.0}}}},"df":0,"docs":{}}},"s":{"df":0,"docs":{},"o":{"c":{"df":0,"docs":{},"i":{"df":1,"docs":{"0":{"tf":1.4142135623730951}}}},"df":0,"docs":{}}}}},"b":{"a":{"df":0,"docs":{},"s":{"df":0,"docs":{},"i":{"c":{"df":2,"docs":{"0":{"tf":1.4142135623730951},"2":{"tf":1.0}}},"df":0,"docs":{}}}},"df":0,"docs":{},"e":{"df":0,"docs":{},"v":{"df":0,"docs":{},"i":{"df":1,"docs":{"0":{"tf":1.4142135623730951}}}}}},"c":{"a":{"df":0,"docs":{},"l":{"df":0,"docs":{},"l":{"df":1,"docs":{"0":{"tf":1.0}}}}},"df":0,"docs":{},"h":{"a":{"df":0,"docs":{},"r":{"a":{"c":{"df":0,"docs":{},"t":{"df":1,"docs":{"1":{"tf":1.0}}}},"df":0,"docs":{}},"df":0,"docs":{}}},"df":0,"docs":{}},"o":{"df":0,"docs":{},"m":{"df":0,"docs":{},"p":{"df":0,"docs":{},"o":{"df":0,"docs":{},"n":{"df":4,"docs":{"0":{"tf":1.0},"1":{"tf":1.0},"2":{"tf":2.0},"3":{"tf":1.0}}}}}},"n":{"c":{"df":0,"docs":{},"e":{"df":0,"docs":{},"p":{"df":0,"docs":{},"t":{"df":1,"docs":{"0":{"tf":1.4142135623730951}}}}}},"df":0,"docs":{},"t":{"a":{"df":0,"docs":{},"i":{"df":0,"docs":{},"n":{"df":1,"docs":{"2":{"tf":1.0}}}}},"df":0,"docs":{}}}}},"d":{